# oracle: comm_modify group with atom_modify first: only the atoms of the group are sent as ghosts (src/comm_brick.cpp
# Comm::borders), so the type 2 atoms outside it have no periodic images and their pairs across the boundary are
# missing (pe -3.058 at step 0 against -3.483 without comm_modify group, measured with native LAMMPS). The 1-2 pairs
# are excluded, so no pair joins an atom outside the group to the image of a group atom.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-10
units lj
atom_style atomic
atom_modify first g1
lattice fcc 0.8442
region box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box 2 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass * 1.0
set type 1 type/ratio 2 0.5 12345
group g1 type 1
velocity all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
pair_coeff 2 2 1.0 1.0 2.5
pair_coeff 1 2 0.0 1.0 2.5
neigh_modify exclude type 1 2
comm_modify group g1
fix 1 all nve
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press pxx pyz
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 10
run 50
